    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #198\n\n- 2026-09-18 06:53Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-18 07:35Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #435 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-198-mail-live-sync-04-06-add-validated-mic-thr_ymid5khx9v` on `origin`. ## Summary Implements issue #198 — validated Microsoft Graph webhook synchronization for mail live-sync: - **`0041_graph_webhook_client_state.sql`**: additive migration adding `graph_client_state` to `mail_account_sync_state` and a unique partial index on `graph_subscription_id`. - **`graphWebhookLifecycle.ts`** + **`graphSubscriptionClient.ts`**: registers and renews a per-account Graph `/subscriptions` REST subscription (daily renewal, well inside Graph's ~2.94-day max lifetime), restart-safe — always re-derives state from the DB rather than memory — and falls back to a fresh registration (with a freshly generated `clientState`) when a renewal reports the subscription no longer exists. - **`graphWebhookNotifications.ts`**: `handleGraphChangeNotification` maps an inbound `subscriptionId` back to its account, validates `clientState` with a constant-time comparison, and hands off to the existing idempotent `enqueueMailAccountSync` job — reusing `graphReconcile.ts`'s already-implemented deltaLink/full-resync path rather than duplicating it. - **`graphWebhookHandler.ts`**, wired into `app.ts` and documented in `routeMatrix.ts`: `POST /api/mail/graph/webhook` echoes the validation token as plain text before any body parsing (well under the 3s requirement), caps and validates the notification body, and always responds `202` to Graph regardless of individual notification outcomes (so Graph doesn't treat a rejected notification as a delivery failure). Tests: `graphWebhookLifecycle.test.ts` (11 tests — first registration, restart/renewal reuse, 404-triggered re-registration, renewal cadence, stop() halting the loop, immediate reconcile on start, notification dedup/rejection) and `graphWebhookHandler.test.ts` (10 tests — validation handshake timing, request parsing, all response-code paths). Full `backend` `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, unit, pi-import-paths, migration numbering, write-safety, dependency boundaries, integration, e2e) passed clean. No `web/` changes were needed. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-18 08:12Z — Relay BB run failed. Reason: Worker ended its turn 3 times without finishing the step (no Relay-Step-Status line) I'll wait for the background wait-loop's completion notification for the `pnpm run verify` run before reporting status.",
